+      # the surviving rows and hence the loss are bitwise unchanged, and the
+      # discarded half stops paying for a full-width fp32 LayerNorm and a vocab
+      # projection whose output is thrown away.
+      #
+      # The GRADIENTS are not. `grad_weight` is a reduction ACROSS rows: the
+      # old path sums 2L rows of which the second L contribute exactly zero,
+      # the new path sums L. Adding exact zeros is exact, but it moves the
+      # blocked GEMM's chunk boundaries, so the nonzero terms are grouped
+      # differently. Measured: 1.11e-16 on
+      # `output_layer.linear.weight` at float64, forward bitwise
+      # (scripts/smoke/fix_equivalence.py --cases f5f6-dit). That is one ULP,
+      # and it is a training-trajectory change, not an inference change --
